   "text": "Drexel University (Postgraduate) - QS Apply\nSkip to main content\nHOMEPAGE\nAPPLICATIONS\nNOTIFICATIONS\nEK\nDrexel University (Postgraduate)\nSummary\nDegrees and Programs\nStudent Testimonials\nCommission\nViewer Access\nAny user can see this institution.\nDescription\nThe College of Engineering at Drexel University is an academically comprehensive global institution preparing students for careers in research, employment in industry or in academia. The College offers more than 25 programs in graduate level study. When you study with us, you will work side by side with today’s top researchers to discover new technologies and seek scientific advances that are applicable to the global challenges addressed by engineers. The college also offers coursework and programs aimed at preparing engineers for leadership and management of technical projects in business and industry.\nTimestamps\nUpdated\n30/04/2026 12:34\nby Gunia Beniwal\nCreated\n26/03/2026 12:42\nby Gunia Beniwal\nType\nUniversity\nPREMIUM INSTITUTION\nCountry\nUnited States\nYearly Fees\nMax: US$13,240.00\nMin: US$1,324.00\nInternational Students\nPercentage of International Students\n20%\n1,673 of 8,367 Total Students\nOverview\nBasic Details\nInstitution Details\nOwnership\nPrivate\nProvider\nDirect QS\nFounded Year\n1891\nCampus(es)\nPhiladelphia\nCountry\nUnited States\nExcluded Countries\nNA\nPREMIUM INSTITUTION\n Yes\nContract Start Date\n01/01/2023\nContract End Date\n31/12/2026\nContract Entity\nQSSA Ltd\nContract Status\nActive\nContract Document Link(s)\nN/A\nImages\nImages\nAdditional Details\nAccommodation Details\nhttps://drexel.edu/drexelcentral/cost/housing/\nScholarship Offered\nhttps://drexel.edu/engineering/admissions/graduate/graduate-student-fellowships/\nYouTube Video Link(s)\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AepSg0Kp1S4\nInternship Details\nhttps://drexel.edu/engineering/partners/overview/\nAdditional Information\n1. Application Fee - USD 65\n2. Please be advised that, in order for a commission to be claimed, the student must remain in good academic standing, which requires maintaining a cumulative GPA of 3.0 or higher. Failure to meet this academic requirement may result in the forfeiture of commission eligibility.\n3. Tagging must be done at point of application, not after submission.\n4.  Student must complete two consecutive terms.",
